# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rule for the web guest client (PLAN_CONCURRENCY.md
# §7/§15). GuestApp.jsx does its own client-side parsing of the path
# (/join/<roomId>) and fragment (#key=<key>) — window.location.pathname/hash
# are unaffected by a Pages "200 rewrite" (unlike a 301/302 redirect, the URL
# in the browser's address bar never changes, only which file gets served).
#
# A single catch-all is correct and sufficient: any path — /join/xyz, a bare
# "/", a typo — serves collab.html, and GuestApp.jsx's own logic already
# handles "no room/key in the URL" gracefully (a clear "this link looks
# incomplete" message, not a crash), so there's no need for a narrower
# /join/* -specific rule.
/*  /collab.html  200
